{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/843135-pittsburgh-cofd-group-looking-for-more","id":843135,"title":"Pittsburgh: CofD group looking for more","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-06T14:12:40-08:00","id":843135,"title":"Pittsburgh: CofD group looking for more","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cross-post from RPG.net</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">We have three people who are experienced roleplayers and have varying degrees of experience storytelling Onyx Path / White Wolf rpgs, and we're looking to round out the group with 1-3 additional players who are still interested in gaming around a table in an area that seems very Pathfinder and D&amp;D-focused.<br /> <br /> We have GMs that are each interested in running a different one of the three &quot;core&quot; games at some point: Vampire, Werewolf, and Mage. We've been talking about using a somewhat shared setting for those games and rotating between them as seems organic to the individual chronicles, so that we can reference events and have an easier time populating the game world. We might start with a mortals game set in the early 80's, and then each storyteller can choose whether to use parts of it or not in their own chronicles taking place in various times following that initial story and in different places in the same general region.<br /> <br /> We're all adult professionals, probably looking at weekend gaming, although evenings could be a possibility. Tolerance and inclusion are a must. While the themes of the Chronicles of Darkness may take characters to uncomfortable places, we never want that discomfort to extend to players at the table feeling uncomfortable.</div> </div> </div> </div>We met up in a thread here started up by another user on the OPP boards late last year, but I wanted to distinguish ourselves from that thread because we\u2019re no longer individual gamers looking for a group, but a group with solid plans to game once we can find a few additional players. We might have a fourth potential player, but one that has a lot of important life commitments at the moment that might get in the way of regular gaming so we want another, and maybe a couple more, people to begin with. So I wanted to circle back here in our efforts to find those last few roleplayers.<br /> <br /> Our current plan: I\u2019m the ST that would probably be running the mortals CofD game, and I\u2019m interested in telling a few stories dealing with ephemeral encounters (with characters less capable in that arena than werewolves), human cults, the intersections between realms and realities, and winding up in places you never planned to be in. This would build up a foundation for an eventual Mage game, but while I wait for the 2<sup>nd</sup> edition of that game to release and to get up to speed with it, we\u2019ll probably spin off to a Vampire or Werewolf game run by one of our other two players. Then we\u2019ll cycle between storytellers as the group wants or needs to change things up.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10592-phlox","name":"Phlox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T09:22:11-07:00","id":913438,"title":"","content":"I sent you a PM already, so you'll find more information there but I would like to join a group yes. Mostly for Mage (either tAsc 20 or tAw 2nd, and if Vampire then masquerade 20 or any other edition)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8022-kinok0","name":"kinok0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}